					"description": "The login API is vulnerable to denial-of-service attack, targeting the hashing function on the server that is used when validating a user supplied password (or in this case a PAN). The vulnerability at the API level exists because there is no maximum limit enforce on the length of the PAN string.\n\nNote: the hashing function used in the demo app has built in protections against large input value. So don't try to actually create a DOS on your own machine! But you can show that the API is vulnerable, because it accepts very long input strings.\n\n\"certain implementations of hashing algorithms may cause [long password denial of service](https://www.acunetix.com/vulnerabilities/web/long-password-denial-of-service/).\"\n\nreference: [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authentication_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authentication_Cheat_Sheet.html)"
				},
